      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2 id="choices">Your choices and rights</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Sign out.</strong> In Settings, choose Sign Out. This ends your session on Nest and asks your account server to revoke Catbird’s access.</li>
    <li><strong>App lock.</strong> Turn on Face ID or Touch ID in Settings &gt; Privacy &amp; Security to require it when you open Catbird. It’s off by default.</li>
    <li><strong>Embedded media.</strong> In Settings &gt; Content &amp; Media &gt; External Media Preferences, choose Ask Before Playing, Always Allow or Always Block for each provider.</li>
    <li><strong>Notifications.</strong> Choose which notifications you get in Settings &gt; Notifications, or turn them off in the iOS Settings app.</li>
    <li><strong>Search.</strong> You can hide Catbird’s content from Search in the iOS Settings app.</li>
    <li>
      <strong>Requests about your data.</strong> You can ask us for a copy of the data Catbird’s servers hold about you, to correct it, or to delete it. Email{' '}
      {email ? <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a> : <Pending label="contact email" />}{' '}
      and tell us your handle. We may ask you to confirm that you control the account.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Depending on where you live, you may also have the right to restrict or object to how your data is used, to receive it in a portable format, to withdraw consent, and to complain to your local data protection authority.
  </p>
  <p>
    Your posts, follows and profile are managed by your account server, and your direct messages by Bluesky’s chat service, not by Catbird. You can change or delete them in Catbird or any other Bluesky app.
  </p>

  <h2 id="deletion">Deleting your data</h2>
  <h3>Your Bluesky account</h3>
  <p>
    Your account belongs to your account server, so deleting it is done there; Catbird can’t do it for you. For accounts hosted by Bluesky, you can delete your account in Bluesky’s own app. In Catbird you can deactivate your account in Settings &gt; Account, and delete your Bluesky chat account with Delete Chat Account in Chat Settings, from the menu in the Messages tab.
  </p>
  <h3>Data on Catbird’s servers</h3>
  <p>
    To delete what Catbird’s servers hold about you (your sign-in sessions, notification registrations and settings, activity subscriptions, thread mutes and muted conversations), email us at{' '}
    {email ? <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a> : <Pending label="contact email" />}.
    Deletion is handled by hand when you ask, and we’ll reply when it’s done.
  </p>
  <h3>The app</h3>
  <p>
    Deleting the app removes its local data. It doesn’t sign you out of Nest or delete anything from Catbird’s servers or your account server, and some Keychain items can remain on the device.
  </p>

  <h2 id="children">Children</h2>
  <p>
    To use Catbird you need an account on an account server, so you must meet that server’s minimum age. For accounts hosted by Bluesky, that’s set in <a href={BSKY_TOS}>Bluesky’s Terms of Service</a>. Catbird doesn’t collect anyone’s age. If you believe Catbird’s servers hold data about a child who shouldn’t have an account, contact us and we’ll delete it.
  </p>

  <h2 id="international-transfers">International transfers</h2>
  <p>
    Catbird’s servers are hosted by Netcup. The location of the data center is{' '}
    <Pending label="data center location" />. Crash and performance reports are processed by Sentry in the United States. Your account server, Bluesky’s services, Apple and Cloudflare may process data in other countries under their own policies. Using Catbird means your data may be handled outside the country you live in.
  </p>

  <h2 id="changes">Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    When this policy changes, we’ll publish the new version on this page with a new effective date. We’ll announce significant changes in the app or on Bluesky at <a href={BLUESKY_URL}>@{BLUESKY_HANDLE}</a> before they take effect. Features that handle data differently from what’s described here will be added to this policy before they ship.
  </p>

  <h2 id="contact">Contact</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Email: {email ? <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a> : <Pending label="contact email" />}</li>
    <li>Post: {LEGAL.controllerName && LEGAL.postalAddress ? <>{LEGAL.controllerName}, {LEGAL.postalAddress}</> : <Pending label="legal name and postal address" />}</li>
    <li>Bluesky: <a href={BLUESKY_URL}>@{BLUESKY_HANDLE}</a> (for general questions; send data requests by email)</li>
  </ul>
</LegalLayout>
